    "review20261024": "Source adds guarded accepted-state document.exportAudio on both platforms, with shared WAV rendering and native atomic publication. Inventory reviewed; runtime qualification pending. See AUDIO-EXPORT-2026-10-24.md. No parity/performance gate is waived.",
    "review20261028": "Advanced gate PR: the five native-command enumerations and nativePatternCommand definition accept gate/gate-stop, with typed target, range, timing, shape and binding constraints. The method inventory and existing vector expectations are unchanged. Both adapters use the shared command validator and stable parameter-binding rules. Gate session, socket, persistence and rendered-audio tests were added; Windows native runtime qualification remains pending.",
    "macParityReview20261028": "Adds the existing Windows audio.devices.get, audio.settings.get/set and midi.devices.get, midi.settings.get/set workflows to the shared schema and Mac adapter. Device identifiers remain platform-specific. Separate settings revisions, dry-run/no-op and strict invalid-input guards are tested by mac/Tests/test_mac_parity.py. No broader parity claim.",
    "macParityReview20261030": "Adds workspace.keyboard.set with expectedKeyboard guarding, lower/upper note mappings and Play/Stop command binding. Source inventory updated; native socket and UI qualification remain pending.",
    "review20261030Audio": "Mark Core Audio settings and device inventory application-only: the windowless TrackerSession host does not own the audio device.",
